{
  "title": "AGTTM Part 6 - Field Staff Implementation",
  "abstract": "AGTTM Part 6 is a practical implementation guide for field personnel involved in setting up, monitoring, and removing temporary traffic management. It translates the technical requirements of other AGTTM parts into practical on-site procedures.\n\nThe guide covers the day-to-day activities of traffic management crews including pre-start checks, equipment inspection, signage installation sequences, ongoing monitoring requirements, and pack-down procedures. It provides step-by-step guidance for common tasks and decision-making frameworks for unexpected situations.\n\nThis part is particularly valuable for Traffic Controllers and traffic management crew members. It addresses practical considerations like positioning of vehicles, communication methods, dealing with public inquiries, and responding to incidents. The guide complements formal training by providing a reference for field implementation of traffic management requirements.",
